  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the light. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell through D2." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f5a929d4-6009-51e2-942a-6c4a853dbaf3"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 39.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "47f27e50-2bf3-52fb-9d0e-3b545371c351"))
  (text "D2: series cell diode (docs/standard.md section 3). Current can leave the cell, never enter it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 43.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "82371484-7184-59dc-be93-60446f775736"))
  (text "R2, R3: NorthSec's I2C pull-ups (1 k on the original). NOT FITTED by default: the SAO standard has the badge provide the pull-ups. Fit 1.3 k to get NorthSec's function." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f407f994-8e9d-5ff9-86a9-ca93dc19cfeb"))
  (text "If fitted they join SDA and SCL to the badge's own 3.3 V pin (VSAO), ahead of the switch, exactly as on the original: no path from them to the cell or to the light." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 128.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "68775dcc-1a09-515d-9f82-14dfed60f62f"))
  (text "D1: red reverse-mount LED on the back, shining through the board in the middle of the gauze pad, where NorthSec's hand-soldered 1206 LED sat on the front." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c4f8a7bc-4a78-5009-9f2d-bd0fbe710c05"))
  (text "R1 1.3k (the original used 330 ohm on 3.3 V): about 1.1 mA on badge power, about 0.6 mA on a fresh cell after D2." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 135.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a8e44f1d-e249-5b52-8f6b-c272347fa2ab"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
